 "text": "Hitchcock County Assessor\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nHome\nCounty\nAbout\nMore History\nVisitors Committee\nOffices\nAssessor\nAssessor's Office\nProperty Search\n-->\nNebraska Taxes Online\nAttorney\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard Members\nMeeting Agenda\nMeeting Minutes\nBoard of Equalization\nBoard Members\nMeeting Agenda\nMeeting Minutes\nClerk\nClerk's Office\nBirth Certificate Info\nMarriage License\nMilitary Discharge\nProperty Valuation Protests\nSpecial Licenses\nClerk of the District Court\nDistrict Court Office\nCourt Filing Fees\nSelf Help\nCounty Court\nCustodian\nEconomic Development\nElection Commissioner\nElection Commissioner's Office\nSecretary of State\nLocal Election Results\nEmergency Manager\nExtension Office\nHighway Department\nPlanning and Zoning\nPlanning and Zoning\nMeeting Agenda\nMeeting Minutes\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nTreasurer's Office\nBoating Guide\nBoating Registration\nDriver's Exam\nDrivers Licenses\nTitles and Registration\nUnclaimed Property\nVeterans Services Officer\nWeed Superintendent\nCalendar\nContacts\nOffice Links\nOffice Links\nOffice Services\nFeedback\n-->\nAssessor\nPhone\n(308) 334-5219\nFax\n(308) 334-5784\nAddress\nPO Box 248\nTrenton, NE 69044\nLinks\n2025 Levies by Taxing District\nFillable Form 425 Report of Destroyed Real Property\nNebraska Department of Property\nAssessment and Taxation\nNebraska Tax Equalization\nand\nReview Commission\nPersonal Property\nReal Estate\nHomestead Exemptions\nGeneral FAQ's\nPermissive Exemptions FAQ's\nMobile Homes FAQ's\nProperty\nSearch\nProperty\nValuation Protests\nTerra Riggs\n|\nAssessor\n|\nLacey Daniels\n|\nDeputy Assessor\n|\nDuties and Qualifications\nThe County Assessor is an elected official who has the general\nsupervision over and the direction of the assessment of all property\nin his or her county. The duties are prescribed by Nebraska\nStatutes, Rules and Regulations (Chapter 77), which have the effect\nof law. The following is a partial list of those duties:\nValuation of real and personal locally assessed property\nwith the county.\nAdminister the assessment statutes of Nebraska law.\nEstablish and maintain fair and equitable value on all real\nand personal property within the county.\nReview all applications for religious, charitable and\neducational tax exemptions.\nMaintain cadastral records (i.e., parcel maps) on all\nproperty in the county.\nPrepare abstract of value and certification of taxes levied\nfor State Property Tax Administrator.\nPrepare annual tax roll for the County Treasurer.\nThe County Assessor must hold and maintain a valid\ncertificate.\nGeneral Information Available from this office:\nTax district information on a property in Hitchcock County\nOwnership records\nEligibility information on Homestead Exemptions\nProperty Inspection Cycles\nHitchcock County Assessor Soil Types Report\nProperty Tax Exemptions\nCharitable facilities\nEducational facilities\nReligious facilities\nHomestead Applications approved by Department of Revenue and County Assessor\nCopyright © 2012 MIPS Inc. All rights reserved. |\nDisclaimer\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate",
